    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0245" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/150</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1917</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 18, 4.50
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1624. [For] Willard [from Stevens]:</p>
                <p>Spare parts for all new decapods should come with these decapods, those most
                    important first. Schulenberg<anchor n="2" xml:id="d286-f1"
                    /> and Lipets<anchor n="2" xml:id="d286-f2"/> should so arrange. Where are the
                    375 decapods on old Russian order? They were to have been ready for Shop
                    delivery last April. Cable quick if any have been shipped from Pacific ports and
                    about when such shipment will be completed.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Francis</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
